  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This paper evaluates gate-based quantum machine learning classifiers on two binary finance datasets using 2 qubits on simulators only: the UCI credit-card default dataset (30,000 rows, 25 features) and a fraud dataset (20,468 rows, 114 features). The key quantitative result is that VQA with LDA reaches 92.54% balanced accuracy on the UCI dataset, while on the fraud dataset the best classical baseline (CART) reaches 87.28% balanced accuracy and the quantum results are mixed, with VQA-LDA at 83.92% and QSVC-LDA at 80.67%.",
